-- =====================================================================
-- Demo: three hands-on workshops of the 2569 academic year, from their real
-- posters, announcements and department newsletters (each newsletter is the
-- event's SAR recap poster):
--
--   1057  Web Developer ด้วย Next.js        Sun 11 Jan 2569 (2026), 08.30–16.30
--         newsletter ฉบับที่ 2 (ม.ค. 2569). Its poster says 15–16 Aug 2569 —
--         the Ruby on Rails dates, rooms and times word for word — but the
--         newsletter records it as held on 11 Jan, so that date is used.
--   1058  Web Developer ด้วย Ruby on Rails  Sat 15 – Sun 16 Aug 2569, 08.30–16.15
--         newsletter ฉบับที่ 62 (ส.ค. 2569; it says "Sunday 17", but the 17th
--         is a Monday — the poster's Sunday 16 is used).
--   1059  AWS Academy & Tech Alliance Workshop 2026
--         Tue 18 – Wed 19 Aug 2569, 08.30–16.00, onsite and online;
--         newsletter ฉบับที่ 63 (ส.ค. 2569); poster 3:4, seats onsite 120 /
--         online 80, registration until Sun 9 Aug, as announced.
--
-- All three are for CS and IT students in year 3 and above, finished and
-- closed, with certificates (evaluations and certificates come from
-- seed_certificates.sql, which must run after this file). Speakers are named
-- in the descriptions (events have no speaker field). Next.js and Ruby on
-- Rails belong to the Skill Up Student Project & Professional Growth Program
-- (แผนพัฒนานักศึกษา ภาควิชาคอมพิวเตอร์ ปีงบประมาณ 2569, item 3: 150,000 baht
-- for the year, ผศ.โอภาส); the plan doesn't split that sum, so each event is
-- given a share. AWS ran the AWS workshop, so it has no department budget.
-- The announcements registered people through Google Forms; here they
-- register in the system, so those links are left out.
--
-- Who came: demo students in year 3+ as they were then (for Next.js, in
-- January, that is today's year 4, then in year 3). One no-show each for
-- Ruby on Rails and AWS, chosen among students with no other absence that
-- fiscal year.
--
-- Apply AFTER schema, seed, demo_organizer, seed_blacklist. Safe to run
-- again: it removes events 1057–1059 (registrations, check-ins,
-- evaluations, certificates and SAR cascade) first — then run
-- seed_certificates.sql again.
--   docker exec -i cpsu-etms-mysql mysql --default-character-set=utf8mb4 -uroot cpsu_etms < database/seed_web_dev_aws.sql
-- =====================================================================

USE cpsu_etms;
SET NAMES utf8mb4;

DELETE FROM events WHERE id IN (1057, 1058, 1059);

INSERT INTO events (id, title, description, category, subcategory, program, years, organizer_id, organizer_name, coordinator_id,
  day_mode, date_start, date_end, event_dates, event_times, time_range, reg_start, reg_end,
  attend_mode, place, online_link, capacity, capacity_onsite, capacity_online, budget_planned, budget_other, budget_actual,
  ask_dietary, meals, issue_certificate, refund_method, status, cycle_stage,
  cert_signer_name, cert_signer_title, email_on_register, email_before_event, email_after_event, created_at)
